   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the village law, in relation to the application of certain provisions of law relating to non-resident members of the village of Blasdell volunteer fire department",
    "basePrintNo": "S7388",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7388-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §10-1006, Vil L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7388\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the village law, in relation to the\napplication of certain provisions of law relating to non-resident\nmembers of the village of Blasdell volunteer fire department\n\nPURPOSE: This bill allows the percentage of non-resident volunteer\nmembers to exceed forty-five percent of the actual membership of the\nvillage fire company of Blasdell, New York.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS: Section 1 amends subdivision 7 of section 10-1006\nof the village law which forbids the percentage of non-resident volun-\nteer members in village fire companies to exceed forty-five percent of\nthe actual membership of the fire company. The amendment exempts the\nvillage of Blasdell, New York volunteer fire department from the\nrequirements of subdivision 7.\n\nSection 2 states that this law shall take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: Currently, village law forbids the percentage of nonresi-\ndent volunteer members in village fire companies to exceed forty-five\npercent of the actual membership of the fire company. This negatively\nimpacts village fire companies by making it more difficult to fill their\ntotal membership and leaving fire companies with vacancies which could\nbe filled by the membership of non-resident volunteer firefighters. This\nbill allows the percentage of non-resident volunteer members to exceed\nforty-five percent of the actual membership of the village fire company.\nThis will help village fire companies obtain greater membership and keep\nour communities safe.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: This is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: Immediately.\n\n",
